  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DJ-Cap. Bldg. Public Procurement Reform</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Purposes and Activities 1.1.   The purpose of the Grant is to strengthen the Recipient&apos;s legislativecomma institutionalcomma and manpower capacity in the area of public procurement by: (a) updating the current Procurement Code and harmonizing procedures; and (b) increasing transparency and efficiency in the Commission National des March&#xe9;s (CNM) and improving local private sector&apos;s competitiveness when seeking government contracts.  The activities (the Activities) for which the Grant is given are as follows: Part I:    (a)commacommaModernizing and simplifying the current Procurement Code; and (b) preparation of a national procurement manual for use in procurement financed from the national budget as well as for donors through the provision of technical assistance. Part II:    (a)commacommaStrengthening the institutional framework and the operations of the CNM with a view to improving transparency and efficiencycomma and enhancing its capacity to disseminate procurement directivescomma manuals and standard bidding documents; (b) strengthening the capacity building of internal control institutions in the area of procurement function skills and enhancing coordination between control bodies; and (c) improving the private sector&apos;s access to government contracts by providing a better governance structure under the updated Procurement Code and through private sector outreach workshops.</narrative>
  </description>
